cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Benchmark Verdicts for Analog Ising Machines Invert Under Tuning: A Negative Result and a Reproducible Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A systematic simulation study of a measurement-feedback parametron Ising
  machine benchmarked against discrete Simulated Bifurcation. The competitive
  verdict inverts twice depending solely on which solver receives parameter
  tuning; tuning both gives near-parity. Includes the hashed benchmark instance
  library and a script reproducing the inversion.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Biller"
    given-names: "Shmuel Y."
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/shmuelbiller1/apim-benchmark-study"
keywords:
  - Ising machine
  - combinatorial optimization
  - simulated bifurcation
  - benchmarking
  - negative result
  - reproducibility
